docs/deployment.md:18:The deployment environment supplies one GitHub App credential pair, the rate-limit binding, and one non-secret identity binding. `TOKEN_BROKER_AUDIENCE` is the exact non-empty, non-whitespace, single-line scalar accepted in subject tokens. It may be URL-shaped or opaque. Public hostname and route ownership remain in deployment configuration rather than a Worker runtime binding. The audience and App credentials can differ across deployments of the same artifact; provider trust and authorization policy cannot change without rebuilding it.
docs/deployment.md:22:`@github-app-token-broker/token-exchange` exposes `createGitHubAppTokenExchange`. Its semantic configuration contains the reviewed composition, `{ appId, privateKey, apiBaseUrl? }`, and the explicit `subjectTokenAudience`; it does not expose environment-variable names or infer audience from `Host`. `@github-app-token-broker/fastify` receives only that prebuilt handler plus standard Fastify registration options such as `prefix`.
docs/deployment.md:33:The workspace enables `inject-workspace-packages` so deployed packages contain built artifacts rather than symlinks to source. `pnpm run deploy:smoke` builds a representative real composition and Fastify adapter, deploys it to a temporary production artifact, imports it with Node, exercises `/token`, and type-checks its emitted declaration.
docs/deployment.md:45:7. supply the deployment-owned Worker name, routes, exact `TOKEN_BROKER_AUDIENCE`, GitHub App ID/private key, rate-limit namespace, and Cloudflare credentials
