 43	- `WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_ISSUER`: remote RPC binding to the private
 44	  `workload-identity-issuer` Worker. Its binding properties fix cyspbot's
 45	  workload subject and the broker audience; application code cannot select
 46	  either value.
 47	- `GITHUB_APP_TOKEN_BROKER`: remote service binding to the deployment-owned
 48	  `github-app-token-broker` Worker. cyspbot uses its existing OAuth 2.0 Token
 49	  Exchange endpoint with `fetch`; the broker does not need a second RPC API.
 50	
 51	The internal GitHub App token flow first calls
 52	`WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_ISSUER.issueToken("https://cyspbot.chikachow.org")`, then
 53	posts the returned short-lived OIDC ID token to the broker's `/token` endpoint
 54	as the RFC 8693 `subject_token`. The caller supplies the canonical GitHub
 55	repository `resource` and explicit permission `scope`; the broker remains the
 56	source of truth for normalization, issuer verification, and Token Issuance
 57	Policy. Subject tokens and issued GitHub tokens must not be logged.
 58	
 59	The broker deployment must separately register
 60	`https://workload-identity.chikachow.org` as a trusted OIDC issuer and add a
 61	Permit Statement for the fixed subject and intended repository/scope. The
 62	client binding only supplies transport and does not grant authorization.
 63	
 64	The public Worker Wrangler files declare only local-development and dry-run values. Production domains, routes, resource identifiers, and secret-store references belong to the separate deployment repository.
 65	
 66	## Tests and validation
 67	
 68	The unit project exercises the root response, empty fallback response, bounded body reading, request-body size and status handling, signature/target validation, response mapping, and both Worker factories. Separate Workerd integration projects load each Worker's real Wrangler configuration and entrypoint.
 69	
 70	Use Node 24 and the pinned pnpm version:
 71	
 72	```bash
 73	fnm exec --using=24 corepack pnpm run check
 74	fnm exec --using=24 corepack pnpm run test:coverage
 75	```
 76	
 77	`check` verifies the frozen lockfile, formatting, generated environment types, lint, TypeScript, Knip, unit and integration tests, and both Workers' Wrangler deploy dry runs.

