# github-app-token-broker deployment pipeline

This private repository deploys the public
[`chikachow/github-app-token-broker`](https://github.com/chikachow/github-app-token-broker)
source to Cloudflare Workers. The reviewed source revision is pinned as the
`src/github-app-token-broker` git submodule; public source is not copied here.

The deployment owns its OIDC Provider Registrations, Token Issuance Policy,
Worker entrypoint, one GitHub App, runtime bindings, and the route
`cyspbot.chikachow.org/token*`. The entrypoint composes reviewed TypeScript from
this repository with reusable packages in the pinned submodule. The initial
route handoff from `cyspbot-deploy` was performed manually; normal deployments
now verify the existing endpoint before mutation and again after deployment.

The reviewed composition registers
`https://workload-identity.chikachow.org` with the source package's generic
OIDC profile: RS256 is accepted and no provider-specific claim profile is
needed for the CWI token shape. Its only CWI Permit Statement matches the
stable subject `cyspbot`, the repository resource
`https://api.github.com/repos/chikachow/cyspbot`, and `contents:read`. The
broker continues to use the existing OAuth 2.0 `/token` endpoint; no broker
RPC API or audience change is part of this deployment.

## Local validation

Use Node 24 and pnpm 10.33.0, then run:

```bash
git submodule update --init --recursive
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
node --run source:install
node --run check
node --run source:check
node --run deploy:dry-run
```

The root install resolves this deployment's workspace against the pinned public
packages. `source:install` and `source:check` independently validate the public
repository with its own lockfile. `deploy:dry-run` validates the deployment
contract and bundles the deployment-owned entrypoint with `--dry-run --strict`.
`deploy` repeats that dry-run before deployment. Only the protected production
workflow calls `node scripts/deploy.mjs --deploy-only`.

`node --run endpoint:check` proves two independent production contracts. The
deployment-owned non-secret `TOKEN_BROKER_AUDIENCE` binding and the pinned
action's Subject-Token Audience are exactly `https://cyspbot.chikachow.org`.
Separately, the deployment-owned route and the client's effective Token Exchange Endpoint are exactly
`https://cyspbot.chikachow.org/token`. With no explicit client URL override, the
pinned cyspbot action defaults to that Token Exchange Endpoint.

`node --run probe` sends a deliberately invalid, credential-free `POST /token`
request. A healthy broker returns OAuth `invalid_request`, status 400, and
`Cache-Control: no-store`; the probe never requests or logs an installation
token.

## Source handoff

The source pin, package boundary, and PR #8 acceptance baseline are
documented in [SOURCE_PIN.md](SOURCE_PIN.md). The update workflow uses
`chikachow/cyspbot-app-token-action` release `v0.0.12`, pinned by its immutable
bundled commit `bf8d299cd20f755c47feb733e3c0f56331a4b49e`. It can advance the
source pin only after the extraction commit is reachable from source `main`.

## Production configuration

The protected `production` GitHub environment provides:

- variable `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`
- secret `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`

Until the account variable is configured, successful `main` CI runs leave the
manual production deployment unchanged. Configure the account variable and API
token together to enable steady-state automatic deployments.

Scope that API token only to the production Cloudflare account and
`chikachow.org` zone. It needs Account Workers Scripts Write, Account Secrets
Store Edit (Cloudflare requires Edit to attach an existing secret binding), and
Zone Workers Routes Write. The bound secret itself must include the `workers`
scope. Do not grant unrelated account, DNS, storage, or user permissions.

The production Wrangler configuration binds `TOKEN_BROKER_AUDIENCE` as Worker
authentication configuration. The public endpoint is deployment-owned route
metadata, not a Worker binding, and the Worker never derives trust from a
request URL, `Host`, or forwarded headers. OIDC Provider Registrations and the
Token Issuance Policy are reviewed TypeScript compiled into the artifact; they
are not runtime bindings or remotely mutable configuration.

Cloudflare Secrets Store must contain `CYSPBOT_GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY` in the
configured store. The production configuration binds that secret as
`GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY`; no secret value belongs in GitHub source or Wrangler
configuration.

Workflows map optional `vars.TOKEN_BROKER_URL` to the endpoint validator's
step-local `TOKEN_BROKER_URL`; the source-update workflow also passes it as the
action's `cyspbot-token-url` input. Leave that repository variable absent for
the current production endpoint so the action uses its default. A future
endpoint-only migration may set the override while leaving the audience stable.
Automated source updates require the accepted source baseline and the production
endpoint contract.

See [GOVERNANCE.md](GOVERNANCE.md) for merge gates and [CUTOVER.md](CUTOVER.md)
for the completed initial handoff and rollback procedure.

