./src/github-app-token-broker/docs/service-contract.md:167:Google service account Clients present a [service account ID Token](https://cloud.google.com/docs/authentication/token-types#service_account_id_tokens) issued by the Google Cloud IAM authorization server with Issuer Identifier `https://accounts.google.com`. The shared verifier requires a non-empty string Subject (`sub`), and the Google service-account OIDC ID Token Profile requires the Authorized Party (`azp`) to equal that Subject. Google documents both claims as the service account unique ID for this token type; github-app-token-broker treats that identifier as an opaque string. Optional `email` and `email_verified` claims do not affect authentication.
